<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Black outline around the flight-screen mini-map (operator, 2026-09-12).

     WHY: the map sits over live video with no panel behind it, the same as the HUD readouts
     since the translucent blocks were removed. Its own tiles are pale — a road layer over a
     light background — so its EDGE disappears against a bright scene exactly as the white text
     did, and the map stops reading as a distinct instrument.

     WHY THE SAME WEIGHT AS THE TEXT: hud_text_outline_width is the one per-device value the
     whole HUD uses for its edge, so the map, the readouts and the EV slider carry a single
     treatment rather than three values that drift apart. See OutlinedTextView.

     This is the FOREGROUND of flightMapContainer, not of the map view itself. The container is
     what toggleMapSize resizes, thus the outline follows the map to its expanded size with no
     second value to keep in step. A GradientDrawable stroke is inset by half its width inside
     the bounds, so unlike a Canvas stroke on text it cannot be clipped by the view edge.

     Square corners on purpose: the map is a square instrument in a column of square-edged
     readouts, and a rounded frame would read as a card sitting on the video. -->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">

    <solid android:color="@android:color/transparent" />

    <stroke
        android:width="@dimen/hud_text_outline_width"
        android:color="@color/tp_hud_outline" />
</shape>
